"Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Conditional Statements", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about conditional statements.  ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about logic, its principles, and methods in simple spoken and written situations.  Describe the development of software programming in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands key information in simple written and spoken texts about topics related to software programming and its history.   Recognizes basic ideas on programming concepts and programming history in both written and spoken passages.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Verb Can (Permission, Possibility, Ability) in Negative Statements", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Can is a modal verb that expresses permission, possibility or ability in the present. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Use <strong>can</strong> when you want to ask for a permission. </br>For example:</br><i> <strong>Can</strong> I ask a question? </i></br></br>  You also use <strong>can</strong> to talk about possibilities. </br> <span class=\"italic\">For example: <br/><i>I <strong>can</strong> be there at 6 am.</i> </br></br></span>  Finally, use <strong>can </strong>to express ability. </br> For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">She <strong>can</strong> remember every conditional code in Java programming language. </br></br></span>  In order to make the negative form, you just have to use  <strong>cannot</strong> or its contraction form <strong>can't.</strong></br> </br>  For example:<br/><i> She <strong>can't</strong> use Boolean operators.</i> ( She has not the ability to use Boolean operators) ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can't execute the sections of code in a program without using control statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "With decision statements, you can't get a result without alternative execution of instructions.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Conditional Codes in Different Programs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Control statements use certain codes to express a conditional statement according to the different programming language. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The following chart shows the conditional codes that the different programming languages use. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Programming Language</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Conditional Code</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Pascal</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"if (condition) then</br> begin</br>    statements</br> end;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">\u201cC\u201d, C++, Java, Perl</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" if (condition) {</br>    statements</br> } else {</br>     else_statements</br> }\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Oracle PL/SQL</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"if (condition) then</br>    statements</br> else</br>    statements</br> end if;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Basic</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If condition Then</br>    statements</br> Else</br>    statements</br> End If\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "execution", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of accomplishing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Control statements are in charge of controlling the execution of those sections of code you want.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "performance ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the doing of a duty ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It depends on the performance of a logical test that leads the statement to handle certain programming situations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lead  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The logical test leads the statement to handle certain programming situations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "computation  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the result of a computing method ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The condition particle is a Boolean expression that will evaluate if certain computation is true or false.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "iterate    ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to repeat something several times ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know they control and iterate the number of repetitions a code is executed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " if I'm not mistaken", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to indicate you are not totally certain about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If I'm not mistaken, all programming languages use specific statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n1le01ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for information about structure conditional statements in different programming languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify different features useful for me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down a paragraph including those features", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the paragraph with the class", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search for information about structure conditional statements in different programming languages.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify different features useful for me.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write down a paragraph including those features.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the paragraph with the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}]}